meta {
  name: List Sold Staff
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sold-deals/staff
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

script:post-response {
  // Capture a staff id so Create Sold Deal can send a `cancelledByUserId`
  // that actually resolves. Runtime-only var (never persisted to disk).
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    const staff = res.getBody();
    if (staff && staff.length > 0) {
      bru.setVar("soldStaffUserId", staff[0].id);
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns id + name for each staff member", function () {
    const staff = res.getBody();
    expect(staff).to.be.an("array");
    if (staff.length > 0) {
      expect(staff[0]).to.have.property("id");
      expect(staff[0]).to.have.property("name");
    }
  });

  test("never leaks a password hash", function () {
    const staff = res.getBody();
    if (staff.length > 0) {
      expect(staff[0]).to.not.have.property("passwordHash");
      expect(staff[0]).to.not.have.property("roleIds");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /sold-deals/staff — the "Cancelled by" picker (PAC-65 #11)

  ⚠ **Runs first in this folder on purpose.** `Create Sold Deal` sends a
  `cancelledByUserId` captured here, and Bruno runs a folder in `seq` order —
  placed after it, the variable is unresolved and the create 400s on an invalid
  ObjectId, cascading into every request that chains off the new deal.

  The agency's staff, so the Sold wizard can name **who** cancelled a client's
  prior insurance when the answer is `SFA staff`.

  - **Module:** `deal_audits` (the same gate as the rest of this controller)
  - **Permission:** `deal_audits:read`
  - **Data scope:** agency-wide callers see every active user; narrower scopes
    are clamped to the caller's branch.

  ## Why not `GET /users`

  `/users` is gated on `agency:users:read`, which only Agency Owner and Branch
  Manager hold — so a **Producer would 403 on their own picker** while filling
  in the form that needs it. Riding the `deal_audits:read` gate they already
  passed to reach the wizard is the same move
  `GET /crm/service-tickets/assignees` makes for a CSR.

  ⚠ Unlike that endpoint this does **not** filter by role. "Who cancelled the
  policy" can be anyone in the agency, and a role-filtered list would quietly
  make the true answer unpickable.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  [
    { "id": "665f…a01", "name": "Pat Producer", "email": "producer@smithfamily.local" },
    { "id": "665f…b12", "name": "Casey Manager", "email": "manager@smithfamily.local" }
  ]
  ```

  Excludes platform admins and users flagged inactive. Sorted by first name,
  then last. Only `id` / `name` / `email` are returned — never role ids or any
  credential field.

  ## How it is used

  Send the chosen `id` as `policies[].cancellation.cancelledByUserId` on
  `POST /sold-deals`, alongside `cancelledBy: "SFA staff"`. The server
  **re-verifies that id against the caller's agency** before storing it —
  without that check the field would be a cross-agency write primitive, the
  same trap `existingPolicyId` documents. An id from another tenant is a
  `400 Unknown staff member on a cancellation.`

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `deal_audits` module disabled, or missing
    `deal_audits:read`.
}
